  "strategy": "1. **Approach and rationale**:  \n   The **central idea** is to use a multi-resolution optimization approach combined with symmetry exploitation to minimize the overlap integral \\(C_5\\). Unlike previous methods that rely solely on local optima, this approach systematically explores coarse and fine resolutions while enforcing **symmetry constraints** (\\(h(x) = h(2-x)\\)) to reduce the search space. The goal is to escape local optima by dynamically adjusting grid resolution and leveraging smooth surrogate functions for efficient optimization.\n\n2. **Mathematical specification**:  \n   - **Variables**: Represent \\(h\\) on a symmetric grid of size \\(n\\) (even). The reduced variable set \\(x \\in [0,1]^m\\) captures symmetry, where \\(m = n/2\\) for even grids.  \n   - **Constraints**:\n     - \\(\\sum_i h_i \\cdot \\Delta x = 1\\) (integral constraint, \\(\\Delta x = 2/n\\)).\n     - \\(0 \\leq h_i \\leq 1\\).  \n   - **Objective**: Minimize \\(C_5 = \\max_k \\int_0^2 h(x)(1-h(x+k))  dx\\).  \n     - Compute using \\(\\text{max\\_overlap} = \\text{dx} \\cdot \\max(\\text{np.correlate}(h, 1-h, \\text{mode}='full')\\).  \n     - Use a smooth surrogate \\(g_\\alpha = \\alpha \\cdot (\\text{max\\_overlap} - 0.38) + \\text{KL divergence}\\) to avoid gradient trapping.  \n\n3. **Implementation procedure**:\n   - **Start grid**: Use \\(n = 200\\) from `initial_h_values` (if available) and enforce symmetry.  \n   - **Resolution adaptation**: Coarsen grid by half (e.g., to \\(n = 100\\)) if objective stagnates. Retry finer grids (\\(n = 400\\)) for higher resolution.  \n   - **Optimization**:\n     - Use `CVXPY` for constraint enforcement and `SciPy SLSQP` for local refinement.  \n     - Compute gradient using finite differences (\\(\\epsilon = 1e-6\\)) for stability.  \n     - Handle infeasibility by projecting solutions \\([0,1]^n\\) and adjusting sums.  \n   - **Objective computation**:  \n     - `compute_max_overlap(h)`: Cross-correlate \\((1-h)\\) with \\(h\\), scale by \\(\\Delta x\\), and return max.  \n     - `smooth_surrogate(x, alpha=1000)`: Smooth version of the objective to escape local minima.  \n   - **Feasibility projection**: Clip values and adjust sums using iterative distribution.  \n   - **Termination**: If budget exceeded, return best solution found.  \n\n4. **Search choices and useful variations**:  \n   - **Grid sizes**: \\([200, 100, 80, 60]\\) (fine-to-coarse).  \n   - **Resolution change**: When improvement < 1e-4 over 10 steps.  \n   - **Restart**: Sample \\([0,1]^m\\) uniformly for new grids.  \n   - **Surrogate parameter \\(\\alpha\\)**: Start at 1000, halve on stagnation, scale up for variance.  \n\n5. **Compute budget and robustness**:  \n   - **Time**: 600s reserved for optimization; split between grid exploration (~200s) and local refinement (~400s).  \n   - **Resource allocation**: Prioritize resolution changes (30%) over other steps (70%).  \n   - **Fallback**: If grid exceeds budget, return parent solution with objective 0.3808.  \n\n6. **Validation and return contract**:  \n   - Verify \\(0 \\leq h_i \\leq 1\\) and \\(\\sum h_i \\cdot \\Delta x = 1\\).  \n   - Compute \\(C_5\\) exactly via cross-correlation and scale by \\(\\Delta x\\).  \n   - Objectives improved in parent: ~0.3795 achieved in some resolutions.",
